  "id": "COMPOUND:19397 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which (E)-N-Isobutylundeca-2-En-8,10-Diynamide interacts with SK-VLB, a cell line that may be involved in sialylation pathways. The compound is linked to the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, an enzyme critical for the synthesis of sialic acid, which is involved in cell surface glycosylation and immune function. This enzyme is also a target of multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and (1S,2R,7R,9S,10S)-6-acetyl-6'-methoxy-1'-methylspiro[4-oxa-12-azatricyclo[7.2.1.02,7]dodec-5-ene-10,3'-indole]-2'-one, which both target SK-VLB. The shared target of these compounds suggests a possible mechanism of action involving the sialyltransferase enzyme, potentially through inhibition or modulation of its activity. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between the compound and SK-VLB, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
